Engine: Select Race records _old_race before Racial_Option_Screen_ (open fix 5).

STATUS: APPLIED, orion2re 6598052c on orionlayer-local (committed as found
by work order 126, part A, 17 September 2026; row 3 of README's orion2re
table). This file is that commit's diff byte for byte (`git diff
6598052c~1 6598052c`, index line included). Filed by work order 192
(29 September 2026): until then the fix had no patch file, so README's
table named it and tools/version_check.py could not require it.

PROOF (work order 192): the diff applies with `patch -p1 --dry-run`, no
offset and no fuzz, both to its parent on orionlayer-local and to the
upstream base cf4d9617; on the tip 96da4c4d it reverses (offset 21, from
the later commits in racesel.cpp).

It is applied, from ~/orion2re, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_select_race_old_race.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert 6598052c` or
`patch -R -p1`, and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    Accepting a Custom Race could crash the Flag Screen with
    "racesel.lbx [entry 138] could not be found": Draw_Flag_Screen_
    computes the entry as race_index + _old_race * MAX_PLAYERS + 0x22,
    and the stock-race branch of Race_Selection_Screen_ entered
    Racial_Option_Screen_ with _old_race still at the displayed
    portrait (13, the Custom Race one) — 0 + 13 * 8 + 34 = 138. The one
    line sets it to the race chosen (0-12), as the lastrace.rac branch
    already does. There is no marker comment: the line itself is the
    marker, and nothing else in orion2re writes it.

diff --git a/src/game/racesel.cpp b/src/game/racesel.cpp
index 25ebccb1..445c3ec0 100644
--- a/src/game/racesel.cpp
+++ b/src/game/racesel.cpp
@@ -299,6 +299,7 @@ int16_t Race_Selection_Screen_(s_player* plr) {
                         struct_::Copy_Structure_(plr->traits, _race_specials[i], sizeof(plr->traits));
                         plr->race = (uint8_t)i;
                         strlcpy(plr->race_name, MOX::_race_names[i], sizeof(plr->race_name));
+                        _old_race = static_cast<int16_t>(i);
                         fields::Deactivate_Auto_Function_();
                         fields::Clear_Fields_();
                         if (Racial_Option_Screen_(plr) == 1) {
